      "side": 1,
      "message": "This line and line 797 both write 16 bytes (`__m128i`) to the `dst` buffer at a time. This is why `src_w` (one half of `dst_w`) must be a multiple of 8.\n\nAn alternative would be to handle a partial write properly. But I suspect we would also need to handle a partial read. I didn\u0027t have time to look into that.",
      "revId": "4e83716c2897e2355f70e970ae937d2c50a71b81",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9639e1ac_b7e2bdb0",
